%T A400425 3692907361,53711928244,778526782020,12742416962466,208583679951361,
%U A400425 3869393727957230,71251563061002241,1450386427032322852,29895975537663119241,666695171387821956976,15036099560027281612801
%N A400425 Number of permutations of [n] whose distinct cycle lengths have equal multiplicities.
%H A400425 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A400425/b400425.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..450</a>
%F A400425 a(0) = 1; for n >= 1, a(n) = n!*Sum_{d|n} [x^(n/d)] Product_{j=1..n/d} (1 + x^j/(d!*j^d)).
%F A400425 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} A400421(n,k).
%e A400425 For n = 4, the possible cycle types are 1^4, 2^2, 4, and 1 3, contributing 1, 3, 6, and 8 permutations, respectively. Hence a(4) = 18.
%Y A400425 Row sums of A400421.
%Y A400425 Cf. A047966 (analogous sequence for integer partitions).
%K A400425 nonn,new
%O A400425 0,3
